{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"d3b8a4ad-1fd0-4e74-89c6-23c600ac18bb","runId":"6df31780-d744-4861-b63c-10444061fa07","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":19,"previousEventHash":"sha256:4b986438618924bf5951710361d02a546a7dd5d87dd92eadf46d51bde279a993","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043a0-1619-79aa-908b-82530636b6dd","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T14:33:05.224Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:209:0292df77-f236-459f-b674-ec4ac9bc8bce","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:209:0292df77-f236-459f-b674-ec4ac9bc8bce","digest":"sha256:b2e22d4551055d8faf9b47627e1decd9d3ce24260d0c7b409dae1e532378e074"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"debcf5b8-613d-448a-b8a3-b14817baa152","runId":"6df31780-d744-4861-b63c-10444061fa07","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:dd6add44cfebb0e5ced68de5756f5f5a74d78d6a9fd4197c752f56ac42f36abf","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043a0-1619-79aa-908b-82530636b6dd","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T14:33:53.062Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":["The existing production guard makes a production edit unnecessary.","The adapter test suite has a reusable transport fake whose request count can prove fail-before-I/O behavior.","The required bound verification command is `check`."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nAdd focused regression coverage proving `setWorkflowLabel` rejects malformed issue numbers before any GitHub transport request. Preserve the already-correct production implementation.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- No changes to `src/adapters/github-projection.ts`.\n- No GitHub API, workflow-label, configuration, dependency, or artifact-schema changes.\n- No unrelated test refactors.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Only positive safe integers reach GitHub issue API path construction.\n- Invalid issue numbers fail before transport I/O.\n- Valid lifecycle-label behavior remains unchanged.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Validate the finding against the frozen integration base.\n- [x] Avoid unnecessary production changes.\n- [ ] Add focused malformed-input regression coverage.\n- [ ] Pass required `check` verification.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact committed head.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\nIssue #209 derives from PR #199 security finding `security-001`. Frozen staging base `6a8af2aaccf459b3ab45208032334e50a9ce629d` already validates issue numbers in both `setWorkflowLabel` and `#replaceWorkflowLabel`.\n\n### Callers And Data Flow\n\n`setWorkflowLabel` validates, delegates to `#replaceWorkflowLabel`, and the helper validates again before constructing issue and labels paths used by the transport.\n\n### CI Surface\n\nThe bound `check` command runs TypeScript typechecking and the full Node test suite. Coverage belongs in `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts`.\n\n### Prior Findings And Hazards\n\nThe original reviewer identified runtime values bypassing TypeScript annotations as the threat. The regression test must therefore simulate untrusted values and verify zero transport access, not merely eventual rejection.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Add request-count instrumentation to the existing projection transport fake.\n2. Add table-driven malformed issue-number cases, including a path/query-shaped runtime string and unsafe numeric values.\n3. Assert every case rejects with the established error before any request occurs.\n4. Run `check`, commit the test-only change, prepare the PR, and launch fresh correctness and security reviewers at the frozen head.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"sha256:plan-209-test-only-regression"}}
